.TH BILTOO 1 "2026-09-15" "biltoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
biltoo \- Qt image viewer with Image, Gallery, and Workspace modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biltoo
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR|\fIdir\fR|\fIproject\fR\&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biltoo
is a classic Qt 6 desktop image viewer with three presentation modes on one
canvas:
.TP
.B Image
Browse one file at a time \(em zoom, pan, rotate, flip, crop, slideshow.
.TP
.B Gallery
Session overview in packed layouts (strip, grid, masonry, and related).
.TP
.B Workspace
Free-form multi-image canvas for comparison, framing, and export.
.P
Sessions can be opened from files, directories, or archives (zip, tar variants,
7z, rar when thumtoo backends allow). Projects use the
.B .biltoo
format (session identity, appearance, Workspace poses, content addressing).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Expand directories recursively when a directory argument is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-start\-at= N
Start at the
.IR N -th
image (1-based).
.TP
.BI \-\-sort= name|path|mtime
Sort the session by name, full path, or modification time.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode= image|gallery|workspace
Initial view mode.
.TP
.B \-\-slideshow
Start a slideshow after loading images.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval= ms
Slideshow dwell time in milliseconds (default 3000).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen.
.TP
.B \-\-thumbnails
Force the thumbnail bar (filmstrip) on.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-thumbnails
Force the thumbnail bar off.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Verbose diagnostics: slideshow traces, libexiv2 metadata warnings, and
thumtoo task traces (same effect as enabling the corresponding environment
variables).
.TP
.B \-\-thumtoo\-debug
Trace thumtoo ladder/tile work to stderr and
.IR ~/.cache/biltoo/thumtoo-debug.log .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
None of the following are required for normal use. Flag-style variables are
treated as on when non-empty and not
.BR 0 ,
.BR f / F ,
or
.BR n / N .
.SS Debug traces
.TP
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG
Enable thumtoo ladder/tile/interest traces on stderr and the debug log under
the biltoo cache directory. Also enables some biltoo load-path traces.
.TP
.B BILTOO_THUMTOO_DEBUG
Alias for
.BR THUMTOO_DEBUG .
.TP
.B BILTOO_LOAD_DEBUG
Extra ImageView load-pipeline timestamps.
.TP
.B BILTOO_DEBUG_SLIDESHOW
Slideshow transition and handoff traces.
.TP
.B BILTOO_DEBUG_FILMSTRIP
Filmstrip (thumbnail bar) schedule diagnostics.
.TP
.B BILTOO_DEBUG_DROP
Drag-and-drop / session-append logging.
.TP
.B BILTOO_DEBUG_CROP
Crop-mode geometry diagnostics.
.TP
.B BILTOO_DEBUG_APPEARANCE
Session appearance / materialize logging.
.TP
.B BILTOO_PERF
Paint and decode-window timing.
.TP
.BR THUMTOO_DEBUG_OVERLAY " / " BILTOO_DEBUG_OVERLAY
Stamp a tiled watermark and border on decoded samples.
.SS Concurrency
.TP
.B BILTOO_THUMTOO_PIXEL_JOBS
Max concurrent thumtoo pixel requests (1\(en16, default 8).
.TP
.B BILTOO_GALLERY_DECODE_CONCURRENCY
Concurrent Gallery soft-decode workers (1\(en32).
.TP
.B BILTOO_FILMSTRIP_THUMB_LOADS
Concurrent filmstrip thumbnail loads (1\(en64, default 24).
.SS Paths
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the biltoo cache and
.IR thumtoo-debug.log
(default
.IR $HOME/.cache ).
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset.
.P
A full table lives in the source tree at
.IR docs/ENVIRONMENT.md .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/biltoo/biltoo.conf
Qt settings (geometry, preferences). Dock
.B windowState
is not restored on some Qt 6.11 builds.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/biltoo/
Durable cache and optional
.IR thumtoo-debug.log .
.TP
.I $prefix/share/applications/biltoo.desktop
Desktop entry (MIME types for common images and archives).
.TP
.I $prefix/share/metainfo/biltoo.metainfo.xml
AppStream metadata.
.TP
.I $prefix/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/biltoo.svg
Application icon.
.SH NOTES
Requires Qt \(>= 6.9. Optional features (libvips, libexiv2, archive/PDF/DjVu
backends via thumtoo, gio-unix default-application Preferences) are detected
at build time and listed under
.BR "Help \(-> About" .
.P
Drag-and-drop onto a window
.B appends
to the session;
.B File \(-> Open
replaces it. Keyboard shortcuts are window-scoped so multiple windows do not
fight for Space, Q, and navigation keys.
